# Gilded Ghoda (2/2 Mount, Saddle 1): on turn 3 an Ornithopter (power 0) alone cannot saddle it (refusal: Saddle 1 needs total power 1 and
# the Mount itself is not "other"); a Mother of Runes cast then can. The saddled Ghoda attacks and "whenever this creature attacks while
# saddled" makes a Treasure (CR 702.171); the saddled state ends with the turn, so on turn 5 it attacks unsaddled and makes none:
# one Treasure in all, and Bot2 took 2 twice (16).

